  "facts": [
    "Opened December 26, 2016, the Ilgaz 15 July Independence Tunnel stretches 5,370 meters in one tube and 5,391 meters in the other, carving a twin‑tubed artery through the Ilgaz Mountains.",
    "Construction began with a foundation stone laid on November 9, 2012, and tunnel boring wrapped up on April 3, 2016, before the tunnel welcomed traffic just months later.",
    "Budgeted at ₺572 million—about US$200 million in 2016—the Ilgaz Tunnel exemplifies Turkey's modern infrastructure push, linking northern provinces with a seamless high‑speed corridor."
